In article <10922@scott.ed.ac.uk>, cavedon@cogsci.ed.ac.uk (Lawrence Cavedon) writes:
> I'm playing as a Samurai and have just cleared out the castle level.
> But when I wish for a cloak of magic protection, the game tells me
> that no such thing exists in the game. Does anyone know what to do---I
> assume that a samurai knows this object by another name; does anyone
> know what it is?? :-(

    Sorry, but from my own experience, you have to identify and an item 
before you can wish for it. You can't wish for any item that you have to 
identify first, if the game hasn't assigned a description to it yet (ie. 
faded pall, ornimental cope, etc.) or you haven't identified the item you 
can't wish for it by its' name, you can however wish for it by 
description. For example, if find a farmilliar bones pile with some item 
that you know the identity of (Hey, old Fred didn't have a feathered hat, he 
had a helm of brilliance.) you may wish for the item by using the 
description instead (blessed +3 feathered hat).

